According to Semiconductor Insight, the global Bonder market is valued at USD 2.44 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 3.63 billion by 2034, expanding at a 4.5% CAGR during 2026–2034. The 2026 market level is estimated at USD 2.55 billion. Bonders are the precision assembly tools that attach and interconnect semiconductor dies through wire, die-attach and flip-chip processes inside packaging lines run by integrated device manufacturers, outsourced assembly and test providers, and advanced-packaging foundries. Semiconductor Insight reports that hybrid bonding and thermocompression are increasing equipment value per packaging line, while Asia Pacific remains the dominant region because of its concentration of OSAT, memory, logic and advanced packaging capacity. The 2026 edition of the report uses 2025 as the base year, 2026 as the estimated year and 2026–2034 as the forecast period, with all values stated in U.S. dollars.

